From b1cddc53c38997e7bed0a9c61f878ab9a8583924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:47:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: preview the last thinking paragraph while a
 thinking group is collapsed

Agents often end a thinking group with a short note to the user (what they
found, what they do next) that never appears as a reply, so it stays hidden
inside the collapsed Thinking row. Show the group's last paragraph under the
header, muted and clamped to two lines, unless an assistant reply directly
follows and already covers the step.

Claude streams several thinking blocks of one message into a single reasoning
text with nothing between them. When the stream announces a new thinking block
right after another one, the timeline assembler now starts it on its own
paragraph, and absolute snapshots join blocks the same way so nothing is
re-emitted. Without block starts the output is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
